    "subject_name": "Physics",
    "chapter_id": "6160241f1a832a8dea12fbf0",
    "chapter_name": "Magnetic Effects of Current",
    "year": "2022",
    "shift": "shift_2"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The electric current in a circular coil of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> turns produces a magnetic induction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at its centre. The coil is unwound and is rewound into a circular coil of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> turns and the same current produces a magnetic induction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at its centre.<br />The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Magnetic field on the centre of a circular current coil is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math>&nbsp;is number of turns,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi></math>&nbsp;is current and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is radius of loop.</p><p>Now, for,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, magnetic field,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Radius of coil&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Magnetic field,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus, the ratio is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}